<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_ThinkTree_SumpMouseWander.xml   UtinniPatches — SUMP_MECHANICS_1 S4

  Wires RM_JobGiver_DreadAvoidWander (RM_JobGiver_DreadAvoidWander.cs) onto
  every animal in the game via insertTag="Animal_PreMain" — the SAME
  global, safe-by-construction extension point SHIP_VERMIN_MOD_1's own
  RM_ThinkTree_VerminBehaviors.xml
  (src/RimMandrake/CreatureBehaviors/Defs/ThinkTreeDefs/) already
  established in this repo, read in full before writing this file. Safe
  because RM_JobGiver_DreadAvoidWander.TryGiveJob's own first line returns
  null for any pawn whose race lacks RM_DreadAvoidWanderExtension — every
  animal that is not RUT_Placeholder_SumpMouseRace (ThingDefs_Races/, this
  same pass) falls through to its own ordinary wander node, same tick, with
  zero behavior change. A SEPARATE ThinkTreeDef from RM_ThinkTree_
  VerminBehaviors, not an addition to its subNodes — that file belongs to
  SHIP_VERMIN_MOD_1, and ThinkNode_SubtreesByTag (Verse.AI, read in full)
  tries every ThinkTreeDef sharing an insertTag independently, so a second
  Def at the same tag needs no coordination with the first.

  Whole-Def MayRequire: this Def's own thinkRoot instantiates a class that
  only exists when mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards is active — same
  posture RUT_SumpDuskLock.xml (S6, this same folder) already uses for its
  own conditionClass reference.

  wanderRadius set directly in XML on the JobGiver instance (10, INVENTED —
  the spec names no figure) rather than in the class's own constructor,
  matching the established idiom this mod's own RM_CompVaporDrifter.cs
  header already documents: "a concrete kind's ThinkTreeDef XML can tune it
  per the vanilla idiom stock animal wander JobGivers already use (e.g.
  JobGiver_WanderHive's own XML sets <wanderRadius> directly)." RimWorld's
  XML deserializer sets protected fields via reflection regardless of C#
  access modifiers — confirmed by that same precedent already compiling and
  shipping in this mod.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThinkTreeDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_ThinkTree_SumpMouseWander</defName>
    <insertTag>Animal_PreMain</insertTag>
    <thinkRoot Class="ThinkNode_Priority">
      <subNodes>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_JobGiver_DreadAvoidWander">
          <wanderRadius>10</wanderRadius>
        </li>
      </subNodes>
    </thinkRoot>
  </ThinkTreeDef>

</Defs>
